# Phase 7 Walkthrough: Docker, Kubernetes & CI/CD

This phase completes the full DevOps infrastructure for the NSIP platform — from containerization to production-grade deployment.

## 🐳 1. Docker Containerization

### docker-compose.yml (Development)
The [docker-compose.yml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/backend/docker-compose.yml) now orchestrates **13 containers** on a shared `nsip-network`:

| Container | Port | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `nsip-postgres` | 5432 | Primary database |
| `nsip-redis` | 6379 | Distributed cache |
| `nsip-kafka` | 9092 | Message broker |
| `nsip-zookeeper` | 2181 | Kafka coordination |
| `nsip-auth` | 8081 | Authentication & JWT |
| `nsip-claim` | 8082 | Claims lifecycle |
| `nsip-contribution` | 8083 | Salary deductions |
| `nsip-education` | 8084 | LMS & gamification |
| `nsip-event` | 8085 | Event ticketing |
| `nsip-rewards` | 8086 | Points ledger |
| `nsip-saga` | 8087 | Saga orchestrator |
| `nsip-payment` | 8088 | Payment gateway |
| `nsip-review` | 8089 | User reviews |
| `nsip-notification` | 8090 | Omnichannel emails |

Each microservice has a multi-stage [Dockerfile](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/backend/auth-service/Dockerfile) that builds with JDK 17 and runs on a minimal JRE Alpine image.

