## ☸️ 2. Kubernetes Manifests

All manifests live in [`k8s/`](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s):

| File | Contents |
|---|---|
| [namespace.yaml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s/namespace.yaml) | `nsip` namespace |
| [config.yaml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s/config.yaml) | Shared ConfigMap + Secrets (DB, Kafka, SMTP, Stripe) |
| [infra.yaml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s/infra.yaml) | PostgreSQL StatefulSet (10Gi PVC) + Redis Deployment |
| [services.yaml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s/services.yaml) | All 9 microservice Deployments with health probes & resource limits |
| [ingress.yaml](file:///Users/muneeb/.gemini/antigravity/scratch/nsip/k8s/ingress.yaml) | Nginx Ingress with TLS + path-based routing |

Key production features:
- **Health Probes**: Every service has `readinessProbe` and `livenessProbe` hitting `/actuator/health`
- **Resource Limits**: CPU/Memory requests and limits to prevent noisy-neighbor issues
- **Replicas**: Critical services (auth, payment, saga) run 2 replicas; review runs 1
- **TLS**: Ingress configured with cert-manager for automatic Let's Encrypt certificates

